# Bounce with a Time tick

`$Time` notifies Game after Time::update. Game::update lists every field. Ball moves only because Game names a new Ball. Target's `%main` is Haxe: it ticks Time, not Game.

## Schema

```
Game = PlayArea Ball $Time
PlayArea = Rect
Rect = Int/x Int/y Int/width Int/height
Ball = Int/x Int/y Int/dx Int/dy Int/rad
Time = Int/t
```

## Construction

```
[:Game
  [:PlayArea [0 0 800 600]]
  [:Ball 100 100 -3 1 5]
  [:Time 0]
]
```

## Methods

```
Time::update = { [:Time (t + 1)] }

Game::bounceDx = {
  r = playArea.rect.
  if ((ball.x < r.x) or (ball.x > (r.x + r.width))) { -ball.dx } else { ball.dx }
}

Game::bounceDy = {
  r = playArea.rect.
  if ((ball.y < r.y) or (ball.y > (r.y + r.height))) { -ball.dy } else { ball.dy }
}

Game::update = {
  ndx = this.bounceDx().
  ndy = this.bounceDy().
  moved = [:Ball (ball.x + ndx) (ball.y + ndy) ndx ndy ball.rad].
  [:Game playArea moved time]
}
```

## Target

Haxe entry. Drive the clock; Game moves because Time notifies.

```
%main
public static function main():Void {
    var assemblage = gameFactory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(assemblage.toConstruction(0, helper));
    for (i in 0...10) {
        assemblage.time.update();
        trace(assemblage.toConstruction(0, helper));
    }
}
```
